course: dictionary
lesson: 16076
title: Wakefulness and the -ness ending
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wakefulness is the state of being awake. When you are in a state of wakefulness, your eyes are open and your mind is working, not sleeping.
explain: It can also mean being unable to sleep when you want to. «The baby's wakefulness at night kept the whole house up.» Here the baby was awake when everyone wanted to sleep.
explain: Break the word into parts: wake, -ful (full of) and -ness (the state of). Wakeful is the adjective, meaning awake. Wakefulness is the noun for that state.
explain: Wakefulness is a noun you cannot count, so say «wakefulness», not «a wakefulness». Common phrases are «periods of wakefulness» and «wakefulness at night».
fact: Wakefulness means the state of being awake.
fact: Wakefulness can also mean being unable to sleep when you want to.
fact: Wake + -ful + -ness: wakeful means awake, and -ness turns it into a noun.
fact: Your body moves between sleep and wakefulness during a day.
fact: Light and screens can cause wakefulness at night, so many people switch them off before bed.
exercise: «The baby's wakefulness at night kept the whole house up.» What does wakefulness mean here? | Being very happy and full of songs | Being ill in bed | Being hungry before breakfast | *Being awake when everyone wanted to sleep
exercise: Which word means the state of being awake? | *wakefulness | sleepiness | darkness
exercise: What does the ending -ness tell you about wakefulness? | *It turns the word into a noun naming a state | It means not | It makes the word an action you do | It means again
test: «After the storm, Max had hours of wakefulness and could not get back to sleep.» What does wakefulness mean here? | Being asleep for a long time | *Being wide awake and unable to sleep | Being full of energy at the football match | Dreaming about the storm for hours
test: Which word is the adjective meaning awake? | sleepiness | *wakeful | wake up | wakefulness
exam: Which sentence uses wakefulness correctly? | «He ate a wakefulness for lunch.» | «Wakefulness is a red bicycle.» | *«Her wakefulness at night made her tired in class.» | «She went wakefulness to the shop.»
